n","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes the canonical minimum spanning tree (weight, then position, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), a minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices ("},{"code":"minimumWeightMatching","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangle inequality (not checked)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tours read the simple graph, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" documents; nil below three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²)."}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/christofidestour(weight:)-6qvc8"]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Christofides.swift#L140","fileName":"Christofides.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE16christofidesTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_tSZRd__lF","title":"christofidesTour(weight:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"christofidesTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","